WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.234
This is a technical demonstration of EmbedIDE, version 0.1.0-alpha.1.

00:00:04.284 --> 00:00:08.119
Everything in the recorded sections is the real program, not a mockup.

00:00:08.169 --> 00:00:11.057
Waiting time is sped up, and it is always labelled.

00:00:11.107 --> 00:00:14.842
The project is a small C ring buffer, and we will edit it, build it,

00:00:14.892 --> 00:00:16.983
and then let an AI agent extend it.

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:20.760
We start EmbedIDE inside the project directory.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:25.372
The explorer is on the left, the editor in the middle, and the AI panel on the right.

00:00:25.422 --> 00:00:27.901
I expand the source folder and open ring.c.

00:00:27.951 --> 00:00:32.662
Nothing has been sent anywhere, and nothing will be until I press Enter in the AI panel.

00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:36.661
Press F5 to build with the project's compiler, here GCC.

00:00:36.711 --> 00:00:38.734
The build fails: a missing semicolon.

00:00:38.784 --> 00:00:42.558
The problems list shows the error and a warning with file, line and column,

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.401
parsed from the compiler output.

00:00:44.451 --> 00:00:46.935
Enter jumps straight to the line in the editor.

00:00:48.035 --> 00:00:51.033
I append the semicolon, press Escape, and save with colon w.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:53.722
Builds use the files on disk, so saving comes first.

00:00:53.772 --> 00:00:56.008
F5 again, and this time the build succeeds.

00:00:57.108 --> 00:01:01.024
Alt+3 opens the integrated terminal: a real shell in a pseudo-terminal,

00:01:01.074 --> 00:01:03.082
started in the project directory.

00:01:03.132 --> 00:01:06.847
The program runs and prints the values popped from the ring buffer.

00:01:06.897 --> 00:01:08.955
Alt+3 again returns to the editor.

00:01:10.055 --> 00:01:11.228
Now the AI side.

00:01:11.278 --> 00:01:16.530
In the AI panel, slash skills lists what agents get: EmbedIDE's own working instructions and the

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.639
skills that match this project, chosen automatically.

00:01:19.689 --> 00:01:25.144
Slash policy shows the three permission policies: read-only, workspace-write, and approval-required.

00:01:26.244 --> 00:01:28.337
I select the Codex CLI backend.

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:33.172
EmbedIDE needs no API key: it runs the Codex CLI you are already logged in with.

00:01:33.222 --> 00:01:35.590
In agent mode, plain text is a task.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.546
I ask for a peek function, a call from main, a build, and a run.

00:01:40.646 --> 00:01:43.886
The agent reads the files, edits them, builds and runs the program.

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:47.527
Every command with its output and every file change is shown as it happens.

00:01:47.577 --> 00:01:49.238
Codex works in its own sandbox.

00:01:49.288 --> 00:01:50.511
This part is sped up.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:59.115
When it finishes, EmbedIDE shows a summary: files changed on disk, commands run, and time.

00:01:59.165 --> 00:02:02.831
Slash review shows the diff, and slash revert would undo the whole task.

00:02:02.881 --> 00:02:05.617
Files open in the editor are reloaded automatically.

00:02:06.517 --> 00:02:10.490
Back in the editor, the build is already up to date, because the agent built it.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:14.741
Running the program shows the new function at work: it prints the peeked value first.

00:02:16.011 --> 00:02:17.794
Permissions are the other half.

00:02:17.844 --> 00:02:20.660
Here I ask Claude Code to delete the build directory.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:24.514
Deleting data is not something the workspace-write policy allows silently,

00:02:24.564 --> 00:02:26.158
so EmbedIDE stops and asks.

00:02:26.208 --> 00:02:29.448
The request shows the exact command and why it needs approval.

00:02:29.498 --> 00:02:30.293
I press n.

00:02:30.343 --> 00:02:33.818
The agent is told it was refused, and the directory is still there.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:42.482
And what you build can be inspected without leaving the IDE.

00:02:42.532 --> 00:02:47.283
This is the compiled program in the hex view, then the ELF inspector with its symbols,

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.451
then the disassembly of ring_pop, produced by objdump.

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:55.303
The file is only read; editing bytes is an explicit mode with a confirmed, atomic save.

00:02:56.203 --> 00:03:00.873
That was one real session: editing, compiler diagnostics, an integrated terminal,

00:03:00.923 --> 00:03:06.070
an AI agent that edited files and built the project with a diff you can review and revert,

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.472
a permission prompt for a risky action, and a view of the compiled program.

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:12.009
EmbedIDE is an alpha.

00:03:12.059 --> 00:03:17.259
Linux is verified, FreeBSD builds but has not been run, and the native GUI is only planned.

00:03:18.759 --> 00:03:20.436
Try it, and tell us what breaks.

00:03:20.486 --> 00:03:23.673
The repository link and the install command are in the description.
